{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531748-combat-math","id":1531748,"title":"Combat Math","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-29T15:22:38-08:00","id":1531748,"title":"Combat Math","content":"I am currently running my first game using the Chronicles of Darkness engine, although I have a lot of history with other versions of the Storyteller system, and I have to say, the combat math seems... off.<br /> <br /> Defense just seems too good.<br /> <br /> A character's athletics score seems to have a bigger impact on a fight than direct combat skills, and most people are rolling to attack with only a chance dice.<br /> <br /> At one point, we had an ordinary gym rat with 3 dexterity and 3 athletics fighting a werewolf. The mortal just kept dodging, and the werewolf simply could not hit him, as it only had a 9 dice pool to attack compared to his 12 dice pool to dodge. It just seemed silly.<br /> <br /> Is there some rule I am missing? Am I doing something wrong?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, as a tangent, do Changelings have some innate resistance to damage in The Lost? One of my players is a longtime Dreaming player, and is used to being able to soak lethal damage when calling upon the weird. When I explained that Chronicles of Darkness doesn't have soak rolls, he was really pissed off as he felt that it was unfair that Changelings were no better than mortal when it comes to survival.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-29T16:18:08-08:00","id":1531756,"title":"","content":"The game doesn't want you to just sit around trading blows. It's very much meant for combat dice-pools to be low and easily put to a chance die, if you just sit there swing at each other.<br /> <br /> Some of this is a reaction to the first editions of the game, where Defense was nearly pointless and combat was really just &quot;whoever goes first goes all offense and 99% of the time one-shots their opponent.&quot; With the relatively low amounts of Health compared to damage output in the CofD 2e rules, one or two hits can easily end a lot of fights, so low dice pools are still very dangerous. It's just much less certain.<br /> <br /> As to your example, someone with a 3 in both an Attribute and a Skill is generally not just an &quot;ordinary&quot; person. That's a decently experienced professional. In general the assumption is that 4 dice is more of what is an average non-professional or entry level professional would have. So that's already skewing things a bit (and 4 Defense isn't going to be winning against a werewolf with 9 attack dice). If someone is just Dodging all the time, you're also free to use All-out-Attack for+2 dice. So the werewolf vs. ordinary gym rat (before we get into why this fight even justifies the full combat rules and isn't just Down &amp; Dirty combat where you can't use Dodge), should really be 11 dice vs. 8 dice (or a bit higher if both start tossing around Willpower as well). And we haven't even brought in any of the werewolf specific mechanics that can push things farther in the werewolf's favor. So the werewolf is going to win this the vast majority of the time.<br /> <br /> As for the Changeling? It seems a weird complaint. &quot;Calling on the wyrd&quot; means using supernatural powers. Lost have Kith Blessings (ex: the Stoneflesh Kith from the Kith and Kin supplement) and Contracts (ex: Red Revenge from Contracts of the Sword) that can penalize attacks or grant Armor in order to be hardier than normal people. Changelings were never the tanks of either the WoD or the CofD. If you want to make a Lost that can endure a lot of punishments, you just pick the right things; just like Dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-29T16:19:51-08:00","id":1531757,"title":"","content":"Dodging means not having an instant action that turn. That character can't deal damage back to the werewolf. When put against Defense directly, the werewolf should hit 66% of the time. WP brings it up to 88%.<br /> Your problem is likely the action economy. You can't Dodge your way to a victory unless you also have allies that can deal damage on behalf of the gym rat, and outnumbering a tough opponent can actually turn a battle into a cakewalk (barring some unlucky rolls).<br /> <br /> Changelings don't have anything innate, but there's a whole category of protective Contracts to use. (Though the two Contracts that grant actual Armor ratings are both Sword instead of Shield).<br /> <br /> As for the player being pissed off; the problem is his expectations. The best way to handle that might be to straight up tell him that Dreaming and Lost are simply two different games that happen to share title due to their shared influence in folklore. This is unlike Requiem that basically was a remake/reimagining of Masquerade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-29T16:32:16-08:00","id":1531758,"title":"","content":"If your werewolf was one of the Forsaken he would have ignored athletics to defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T07:39:03-08:00","id":1531784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531748-combat-math?p=1531758#post1531758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your werewolf was one of the Forsaken he would have ignored athletics to defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only in Gauru.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T11:30:49-08:00","id":1531790,"title":"","content":"The <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i> core book has a pretty helpful baseline for what skills and attribute dots represent:<br /> <br /> 1- Below average / hobbyists or someone who took an introductory class.<br /> 2- Average human / a trained professional.<br /> 3- Above average / a reference in their field.<br /> 4- Genius level / mover and shaker in their field.<br /> 5- Peak human ability / legendary level of skill.<br /> <br /> So this gym rat has the conditioning to be a professional athlete or a stunt double. Lets assume circumstances didn't allow the werewolf to get the extra Strength die from Dalu form. Using an all out attack to grapple means you are able to almost match them, or exceed their pool with willpower expenditure. All the werewolf needs is for a grapple to succeed and they seize the win.<br /> <br /> They cannot dodge forever and the lowered defense tempts them to retaliate, which can create the opening for the grapple. Will they try to escape or call for help instead or does the werewolf have a plan for that ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T12:06:57-08:00","id":1531791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531748-combat-math?p=1531784#post1531784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only in Gauru.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any fight with a Uratha is likely going to involve fighting Gauru.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T13:12:59-08:00","id":1531797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531748-combat-math?p=1531791#post1531791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any fight with a Uratha is likely going to involve fighting Gauru.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gauru is the killing form and not every fight is to the death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T14:48:05-08:00","id":1531810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531748-combat-math?p=1531758#post1531758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your werewolf was one of the Forsaken he would have ignored athletics to defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not using Forsaken, or any of the splats. Until we get the system down, we are playing mortals using core only. I improvised the werewolf based on my knowledge of W:TA. It was in Hispo form and had a dice pool of nine.<br /> <br /> Out of curiosity, how does the ignoring athletics work in Forsaken?<br /> <br /> [QUOTE=Heavy Arms;n1531756As for the Changeling? It seems a weird complaint. &quot;Calling on the wyrd&quot; means using supernatural powers. Lost have Kith Blessings (ex: the Stoneflesh Kith from the Kith and Kin supplement) and Contracts (ex: Red Revenge from Contracts of the Sword) that can penalize attacks or grant Armor in order to be hardier than normal people. Changelings were never the tanks of either the WoD or the CofD. If you want to make a Lost that can endure a lot of punishments, you just pick the right things; just like Dreaming.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> That is unlikely to sway his opinion. His perspective is that CoD has nerfed his beloved Changelings by removing their ability to soak lethal, and explaining that it is a whole new game set will likely aggravate him further. To me it makes no sense, as the removal of soak seems to have greatly leveled the playing field, and as changelings were already on the more fragile side of the spectrum in Old World of Darkness, the levelling is to their advantage, but the player in question is only comparing himself to mortals rather than other supernatural afaict.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531748-combat-math?p=1531790#post1531790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i> core book has a pretty helpful baseline for what skills and attribute dots represent:<br /> <br /> 1- Below average / hobbyists or someone who took an introductory class.<br /> 2- Average human / a trained professional.<br /> 3- Above average / a reference in their field.<br /> 4- Genius level / mover and shaker in their field.<br /> 5- Peak human ability / legendary level of skill.<br /> <br /> So this gym rat has the conditioning to be a professional athlete or a stunt double. Lets assume circumstances didn't allow the werewolf to get the extra Strength die from Dalu form. Using an all out attack to grapple means you are able to almost match them, or exceed their pool with willpower expenditure. All the werewolf needs is for a grapple to succeed and they seize the win.<br /> <br /> They cannot dodge forever and the lowered defense tempts them to retaliate, which can create the opening for the grapple. Will they try to escape or call for help instead or does the werewolf have a plan for that ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a couple of quibbles with this, on both a mechanical and narrative level.<br /> <br /> The game gives players enough dots to create their characters with that, unless everyone just goes for a jack of all trades with one dot in everything, you are going to have a few abilities at 3+, even if you are going out of your way to make a normal person rather than an expert in their field. <br /> <br /> This is especially true in sports, where everyone has the ability to play casually, but less than a percent of a percent of the population has what it takes to make it in the major leagues. One dot of athletics just doesn't seem like enough to differentiate, say, the captain of the varsity football team from the nerdiest member of the chess team.<br /> <br /> But even if we use the chart at face value and drop the gym rat down to a 2 athletics, his defensive dice pool is now 10, and is still higher than the werewolf's 9. And a three would give him a twelve, equivalent to the world's best mortal swordsman with a 5 str and 5 going all out offense. It just feels wrong that the entirety of the NFL can act like Pei Mei in Kill Bill volume 2 and render highly proficient swordsmen unable to land even a single blow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T15:25:41-08:00","id":1531815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531748-combat-math?p=1531810#post1531810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, how does the ignoring athletics work in Forsaken?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Gauru &quot;wolf-man&quot; form werewolves use as a killing form has a quality called Primal Fear that makes combat with &quot;lesser enemies&quot; \u2014 including most humans, animals, and lower-Ranked spirits \u2014 resolved in a single roll with the Down and Dirty Combat rules, and removes Athletics from the Defense of opponents in normal combat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is unlikely to sway his opinion. His perspective is that CoD has nerfed his beloved Changelings by removing their ability to soak lethal, and explaining that it is a whole new game set will likely aggravate him further. To me it makes no sense, as the removal of soak seems to have greatly leveled the playing field, and as changelings were already on the more fragile side of the spectrum in Old World of Darkness, the levelling is to their advantage, but the player in question is only comparing himself to mortals rather than other supernatural afaict. </div> </div> </div>The system in general doesn't give non-specialists an overwhelming advantage in a straight fight, which is kind of the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The game gives players enough dots to create their characters with that, unless everyone just goes for a jack of all trades with one dot in everything, you are going to have a few abilities at 3+, even if you are going out of your way to make a normal person rather than an expert in their field. </div> </div> </div>There are twenty-four Skills in the game and the way unSkilled penalties work means you're encouraged to prioritize Mental Skills if you at all expect to encounter situations where they'd be relevant. You are given a total of twenty-two dots to put into these containers that fit up to five dots each, and they're split up by category such that you're not going to get e.g. three Physical Skills maxed out at default character creation.<br /> <br /> The game also gives you enough Merit dots to be a millionaire on paper with minor psychic powers, but the assumptions of the game are not that the setting is populated by every possible arrangement of dots on a sheet, much less the optimized varieties.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is especially true in sports, where everyone has the ability to play casually, but less than a percent of a percent of the population has what it takes to make it in the major leagues. One dot of athletics just doesn't seem like enough to differentiate, say, the captain of the varsity football team from the nerdiest member of the chess team. </div> </div> </div>I do not know why you think the nerdiest member of the chess team has any dots in Athletics and the same Physical Attributes as the football captain in this scenario.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But even if we use the chart at face value and drop the gym rat down to a 2 athletics, his defensive dice pool is now 10, and is still higher than the werewolf's 9. And a three would give him a twelve, equivalent to the world's best mortal swordsman with a 5 str and 5 going all out offense. It just feels wrong that the entirety of the NFL can act like Pei Mei in Kill Bill volume 2 and render highly proficient swordsmen unable to land even a single blow. </div> </div> </div>Skill Specialties are the main way characters implicitly manage good normal dicepools without being omnidisciplinary scientists or proficient in every musical instrument. Your gym rat is not necessarily going to have Athletics <i>1</i>, much less 2 or 3, because Athletics represents more than being in shape (which you would instead model with high Physical Attributes).<br /> <br /> Even setting aside the starting points, the reason Dodging doubles your Defense is because a contested dice roll is less certain than a flat penalty when it comes to damage mitigation and you're dedicating your entire action to getting out of the way of an attack to which Defense applies in a system where the first step of combat is declaring what your goal is for the action scene. Dodging means you can't <i>run</i>. It means you can't hit back or bar a door or spring a trap without bringing in extra people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Closing quote tag. 03-01-2024, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T16:39:06-08:00","id":1531819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531748-combat-math?p=1531810#post1531810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not using Forsaken, or any of the splats. Until we get the system down, we are playing mortals using core only. I improvised the werewolf based on my knowledge of W:TA. It was in Hispo form and had a dice pool of nine.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might want to revisit the antagonist building section of the book. A skill mob hitman gets 8 dice to shoot people. A werewolf that has 9 dice to bite people while in a giant monster-wolf form is perhaps not strong enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is unlikely to sway his opinion. </div> </div> </div>It doesn't sound like there's anything to do but perhaps play the game, and when it comes around to expanding to trying other game-lines, you can pick up Changeling and then show off how tough they can be. Words apparently aren't going to help.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The game gives players enough dots to create their characters with that, unless everyone just goes for a jack of all trades with one dot in everything, you are going to have a few abilities at 3+, even if you are going out of your way to make a normal person rather than an expert in their field. </div> </div> </div>And? The ability to start with Dexterity 3/Athletics 3 doesn't change what those traits mean. A base pool of 6 isn't an &quot;ordinary gym rat.&quot; They're in above average shape and an athlete of experience professional talent. These are the stats of someone that regularly wins local triathlons or plays for a low prestige tier professional sports team; not someone that has a solid exercise routine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One dot of athletics just doesn't seem like enough to differentiate, say, the captain of the varsity football team from the nerdiest member of the chess team. </div> </div> </div>A Dexterity 1/Athletics 0 character default to a chance die, while a Dexterity 2/Athletics 1/Specialty: Football, character defaults to 4 dice. Seems like plenty of a differentiation to me.<br /> <br /> With Dexterity 1-2 and Athletics 0-1, you can have a range of base dice from 0 to 4.<br /> <br /> Where's the problem?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And a three would give him a twelve, equivalent to the world's best mortal swordsman with a 5 str and 5 going all out offense. It just feels wrong that the entirety of the NFL can act like Pei Mei in Kill Bill volume 2 and render highly proficient swordsmen unable to land even a single blow. </div> </div> </div>OK, so there's something else. If you're stopping at Attributes and Skills, you're not getting to the best of the best.<br /> <br /> The best swordsman in the world as multiple appropriate specialties and Merits. Look at what things like Professional Training, Area of Expertise, and an appropriate Fighting Style can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T17:35:18-08:00","id":1531823,"title":"","content":"Ok. That makes a lot more sense now.<br /> <br /> Related question about the timing of dodge. Can you declare dodge after an enemy has decided to attack you? If so, can they then change their mind and attack someone else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T17:53:57-08:00","id":1531827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531748-combat-math?p=1531823#post1531823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related question about the timing of dodge. Can you declare dodge after an enemy has decided to attack you?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can Dodge an attack targeting you if you haven't taken an action during the turn yet, and you can delay your action to take it at any later point in the turn, so functionally, yes. Dodge works the same way it did in 1e apart from now being a roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If so, can they then change their mind and attack someone else? </div> </div> </div>If you declare that you are Dodging, enemies are not obligated to try to hit you, but neither does it make any sense for them to be able to go &quot;wait, never mind&quot; after declaring an attack to force you to commit to the action in some sort of lopsided order-of-operations where the Storyteller can change their mind about how to proceed before dice are rolled but the player cannot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T18:10:46-08:00","id":1531829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531748-combat-math?p=1531827#post1531827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can Dodge an attack targeting you if you haven't taken an action during the turn yet, and you can delay your action to take it at any later point in the turn, so functionally, yes. Dodge works the same way it did in 1e apart from now being a roll.<br /> <br /> If you declare that you are Dodging, enemies are not obligated to try to hit you, but neither does it make any sense for them to be able to go &quot;wait, never mind&quot; after declaring an attack to force you to commit to the action in some sort of lopsided order-of-operations where the Storyteller can change their mind about how to proceed before dice are rolled but the player cannot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so this strategy is perfectly kosher?<br /> <br /> Four mortals are fighting a tough monster.<br /> The mortals do nothing, waiting for the monster to attack one of them.<br /> The monster attacks, and his target declares a dodge, meaning that the monster is likely to whiff completely.<br /> The other three mortals respond by doing an all-out attack on the monster.<br /> <br /> Because this is how every combat has gone so far in my game, and it allows a group of ordinary people with combat dice pools of 4-6 armed with baseball bats and pocket-knives to take down monsters with dice pools of 8-10 reliably and without ever taking a scratch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T18:34:21-08:00","id":1531831,"title":"","content":"It depends, if the person has things like 5 dots of <i>Professional Training</i> with Brawl, they get 9-again on related rolls and rote quality by spending Willpower. Now combine that with the <i>Clinch Strike</i> merit, which lets you inflict damage on a successful grapple, if you are lucky to get an exceptional success and choose the damage maneuver, it means you could inflict twice your successes in damage. <i>Body as Weapon</i> adds another point of damage. Five dots of <i>Martial Arts</i> makes their hand do 2 more damage and can now selectively inflict lethal. All with a weapon that can't be disarmed, is great at disabling single targets and can be quite silent. Despite its short range, it also does not reduce initiative, making it quite fast.<br /> <br /> With firearms, use of the Covering Fire maneuver guarantees hits if the target doesn't go prone or running to cover, which is great for setting up traps and flanking.<br /> <br /> Characters can be built to have more options via merits and Fighting Styles. They will be more precise, dangerous and use less Willpower. But just like investigating or being a diplomat, it requires sinking XP to specialize.<br /> <br /> I would recommend the <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i> core book and <i>Hurt Locker</i>, both are great resources for mortal chronicles and flesh out the fighting system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 03-01-2024, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T03:13:38-08:00","id":1531839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531748-combat-math?p=1531797#post1531797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gauru is the killing form and not every fight is to the death.</div> </div> </div> </div>People don't generally include the Uratha in non-werewolf games, then complain about combat math in a fight to first blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T15:34:45-08:00","id":1531855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531748-combat-math?p=1531827#post1531827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can Dodge an attack targeting you if you haven't taken an action during the turn yet, and you can delay your action to take it at any later point in the turn, so functionally, yes. Dodge works the same way it did in 1e apart from now being a roll.<br /> <br /> If you declare that you are Dodging, enemies are not obligated to try to hit you, but neither does it make any sense for them to be able to go &quot;wait, never mind&quot; after declaring an attack to force you to commit to the action in some sort of lopsided order-of-operations where the Storyteller can change their mind about how to proceed before dice are rolled but the player cannot.</div> </div> </div> </div>So far all of our combats have worked out like this:<br /> <br /> <br /> I try and set up a fairly standard monster / slasher movie scenario where something big, scary and supernatural is killing people. <br /> <br /> A group of ordinary people with dice pools of 3-6 armed with pocket-knives and baseball bats encounter the monster with a dice pool in the 8-12 range that looks like it should be able to wipe the floor with them.<br /> <br /> The players wait for the monster to attack, and then whomever it attacks declares dodge, and then almost always misses.<br /> Everyone else then does an all-out attack on the monster.<br /> <br /> The result is that the monster is killed, and the mortals only take a very occasional minor wound.<br /> <br /> Is this how combat is supposed to go in the system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T16:46:17-08:00","id":1531858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531748-combat-math?p=1531855#post1531855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The result is that the monster is killed, and the mortals only take a very occasional minor wound.<br /> <br /> Is this how combat is supposed to go in the system?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a banner example of why monsters run with any intelligence or self-preservation do not attack groups on their own in circumstances where they can see the monster coming. For a predator, straight fights are a sucker's bet.<br /> <br /> If for some reason you still want a monster to be able to solo a PC group in open combat without engaging in tactical behavior, you give it qualities and methods that don't allow it to get eaten by the action economy quite so directly, like invisibility, regeneration, damage reduction, ranged attacks, grappling, projecting an area effect, and so on \u2014 things that bypass Defense and prevent the opposition from hitting you in ways that matter.<br /> <br /> If the monster is not given specific qualities that would logically allow it to survive getting jumped in an alley, it is logically not going to mare any better in that regard than a normal very talented person would in the same situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T17:37:53-08:00","id":1531859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531748-combat-math?p=1531858#post1531858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a banner example of why monsters run with any intelligence or self-preservation do not attack groups on their own in circumstances where they can see the monster coming. For a predator, straight fights are a sucker's bet.<br /> <br /> If for some reason you still want a monster to be able to solo a PC group in open combat without engaging in tactical behavior, you give it qualities and methods that don't allow it to get eaten by the action economy quite so directly, like invisibility, regeneration, damage reduction, ranged attacks, grappling, projecting an area effect, and so on \u2014 things that bypass Defense and prevent the opposition from hitting you in ways that matter.<br /> <br /> If the monster is not given specific qualities that would logically allow it to survive getting jumped in an alley, it is logically not going to mare any better in that regard than a normal very talented person would in the same situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just don't see it as &quot;logical&quot; in any way.<br /> <br /> In a movie, if the camp councilors decided to jump the slasher with baseball bats, I would expect them to die in short order, and in real life if my friends and I decided to go hunt a tiger with pocketknives, I would expect most of us to walk away with serious injuries, if we walked away at all.<br /> <br /> The ability to reactively dodge in response to an enemy's attack just makes the scenario play out in a really weird way that doesn't fit my conception of real life, genre fiction, or combat in other RPGs, to the point where I was sure we were doing it wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26576-talakeal","name":"Talakeal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T18:09:46-08:00","id":1531860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talakeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531748-combat-math?p=1531859#post1531859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't see it as &quot;logical&quot; in any way.<br /> <br /> In a movie, if the camp councilors decided to jump the slasher with baseball bats, I would expect them to die in short order,</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you expect them to commit to <i>blink-tank strats</i>? Would you expect the slasher to be liable to be taken by surprise and have no mitigating supernatural qualities or other abilities in this situation?<br /> <br /> Like, multiple Fighting Style Merits provide means of just <i>passively dealing damage</i> to any opponents within melee range of the character, and Mask slashers reduce damage from individual attacks to one point each. Attributes and Skills just give you dice \u2014 representing the ability to get around the problem of tackling multiple opponents at once is accomplished through other parts of the system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and in real life if my friends and I decided to go hunt a tiger with pocketknives, I would expect most of us to walk away with serious injuries, if we walked away at all. </div> </div> </div>Setting aside that the wild tiger is one of the most threatened species on the planet, you would also presumably not be hunting the tiger in a featureless white room where it doesn't benefit from camouflage, cover, or the ability to run away and wear you down. Again: a straight fight is a sucker's bet for a predator.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The ability to reactively dodge in response to an enemy's attack just makes the scenario play out in a really weird way that doesn't fit my conception of real life, genre fiction, or combat in other RPGs, to the point where I was sure we were doing it wrong. </div> </div> </div>The ability to reactively dodge, again<i>, deprives you of your ability to do anything else on your turn</i>, which matters because common-sense tactics are to get your target alone if your goal is to win the fight on account of how most people have difficulty fighting two or more other people at once.<br /> <br /> Chronicles incentivizes fighting smart, and fighting smart means not fighting fair <i>and also not picking fights that are inherently lopsided in your opponent's favor.</i> If you want to counteract that unfair advantage, the tools to do so do not exist in the systems for <i>basic dicepool construction.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T22:56:44-08:00","id":1531864,"title":"","content":"As an example of how to shake things up 1e actually had a monster specifically designed to murder the PCs if they tried the &quot;one person dodges and everyone else beats on the critter with it's one attack.&quot;<br /> <br /> If killed, it instantly regenerated with improved (cumulatively) stats, because it fed off of lethal violence; even violence aimed at it. It wasn't so strong at first that it would TPK players before they could figure out this trick, but there was no solving it with more heavy violence. They had to pick something else.<br /> <br /> Ephermeral entities which can potentially harm PCs from the Twilight while being completely immune to normal physical attacks are also available.<br /> <br /> You can also just give a slasher-style baddy 5/0 Armor, Regeneration, a good enough stealth pool to ambush the PCs, and a good enough dice pool to attack to hit dodging PCs that standing around trying to beat it with pocket knives and baseball bats is a losing tactic. Though you'll probably kill a few before they do much if you do.<br /> <br /> If you're the ST. You have the tools to make antagonists as dangerous as you want them to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}